# Speech text shaping

Source: SPEC VA-04, VA-08; PLAN Phase 6C.

## Two forms of every assistant reply
- `spoken_text` goes to TTS. `display_text` is the readable written form of the **same words** for captions.
- They must carry identical words and numbers (check V6.5). Captions must show only what was actually spoken;
  an interrupted, never-heard continuation is not presented as spoken.

## Sanitizer
Strip markdown, bullets, URLs, IDs, emoji. Spoken text never contains IDs, URLs, JSON, code or internal status names.

## Verbalizer
- PKR amounts and quantities are spoken unambiguously: "eight hundred fifty rupees", never "eight fifty" or "one fifty".
- Handle ranges, totals, decimals, large numbers, and positions ("the second of four").
- Price or quantity mistakes in speech are **zero tolerance**.
- Text transforms never change meaning or numbers.
- Unit tests: at least 40 cases, including 150 vs 1,500, ranges, totals, decimals (V6.1).

## Pronunciation and chunking
- Dish and brand names: pronunciation dictionary (Cartesia dictionaries if supported by the chosen model, otherwise respelling).
- The first sentence is short so TTS starts early. List items are one per sentence, with natural pauses from punctuation.

## Delivery
- No fake stutters or repeated fillers (R9).
- Default to Cartesia's context-driven delivery. Emotion settings stay off unless the listening test (6E) shows they help.
- Truthful wait feedback: only if an action is pending longer than about 1.5 s, say one short honest status, once
  ("Still checking the cart."). It must contain no success wording; a regex guard enforces this.
- Speed and volume preferences are honored only if the chosen Sonic model supports them (Phase 1 ADR).
  Never claim a capability the voice lacks.
